1 OCCU Överstelöjtnant. Adlades Gyllensvärd år 1632. Överstelöjtnant 1633., Riddare, Överstelöjtnant, Adlig ätt nr 240, Adlad år 1632. Ätt nr 240, äg Önnarp i Hössna, Colonel
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Per Joensson Gyllensvärd till Önnarp and Hössna=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth:	1594 in Hössna, Älvsborg (P), Sweden
2 CONT * Death:  March 19, 1664 in Hössna, Ulricehamn, Älvsborg (P), Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT * Per Jonsson Gyllenswärd's father is probably the Jon Jönsson (Store-Jon) in Svinanäs who is mentioned in the court records at the beginning of the 17th century, and this in turn is possibly the son of the sheriff Jöns Jonsson in
2 CONC  Gavlö known approx. 1575-81, who in turn could be the brother of Per Jonsson to Gavlö, married to Anna Henriksdotter (Gyllensparre).  
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Seat Farm: Önnarp and Hössna.'''
2 CONT * '''Ennobled: 12 August 1632 (shield letter 1648). Peder took the name Gyllenswärd upon introduction in 1638, when the family was assigned number 240. The nobility was finally confirmed in 1647 by Queen Kristina , who signed the 
2 CONC family's shield letter.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * At the Knights House, Åkerstein's notes have given rise to information in the genealogy that his ancestor, Per Joensson, started as a puppet boy and that his father was a "pedestrian" (Åkerstein states: paratroopers) in Västergö
2 CONC tland. A story in »Newspaper from Falköping city and Falbygden» for 30 January. In 1864, a legend states that Per was discharged as a rider from the farm Näbbarp, located in the red road west of Lake Lönern, that he, in a slaughte
2 CONC r, moved the king away from the enemies and the day after that he received the message: "Previously you were called Per Näbb, now your name is Per Gyllenswaard
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000001985522486?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000190256246860 '''RIKSDAGSPROTOKOLL, page 111''']
2 CONT * Per Joensson , Gyllensvärd left, to Önnarp, and Hössna, both in Hössna, the county of Älvsborg. From Sunnerbo, in Småland. Accepted war service 1607, was a fighter at Västbo krektar 1618-03-26 and was 1622 at the Riga Lieutenant
2 CONC  in his brother-in-law Baltzar von Neuman's company of Swag Johan Hindersson Routers of Skälboö Regemente Västgöta Knektar (Skaraborg regemente). The captain of Nils Ribbing's West Govtegemente (Älvsborgs) 1624. Transferred to Väs
2 CONC tgöta rider 1628. Patterned as rider at Smålands rider 1630-06-17 in Kalmar. Admitted 1632-08-12 in the field camp at Nuremberg, but the nobility letter first signed 1634-09-10 and confirmed 1647-04-20 (introd. 1638-01-17 under nu
2 CONC mber 240). Major 1632, at the end of the year. Lieutenant Lieutenant in 1633 and then brought in nine with the top of the treaties commanded over the regiment during the visit of Lützen, Fredrik Stenbock, at home in the country. E
2 CONC xit from the Registry in 1641, when he was not appointed to his Colonel. Head of a nobility company at the outbreak of the war with Denmark in 1644, contributing substantially to the successful outcome of the battle at Önsvalla Pa
2 CONC ss in Halland. Dismissed 1656. Death 1664-03-19 and buried in the midsummer's day in Hössna church. He bought 1626 Önnarps tax warehouse, etc. in Hössna parish, and received 1629-03-03 peace of mind in a pleasant time. In the foll
2 CONC owing three decades he formed through the purchase of the tax and krono home in Västergötland and Småland the seas Önnarp and Hössna as well as Prästtorp in the Berga parish, Kronoberg County. 
2 CONT * Per Joensson Gyllenswaard was born ca. 1594 in Odensjö, and died on March 19, 1684 at Önnarp in Hössna. His father's name was Joen Persson, and he is believed to be from Sunnerbo gentleman and may have belonged to a national bai
2 CONC liff. He did war service from 1607, enlisted in Västbo kntar 1618, lieutenant in muster in Riga 1622, captain of Nils Ribbings Västgöta Regiment 1630 in Kalmar, major 1632, Lieutenant Colonel 1633 and served as interim colonel com
2 CONC mander of the regiment during the Stutzen seaside, until he retired from the regiment in 1641 and became head of the Adelsfanekompagniet at the outbreak of the war against Denmark in 1644. He contributed to the victory at Onsvalla
2 CONC  pass in Halland. Farewell 1656.  He was born in Nuremberg in 1632.  He resigned in 1656, and was the owner of Önnarp farm in Hössna as well as Prästtorp in Berga, Kronoberg County.  He had a brother named Joen Joensson and was ma
2 CONC rried to Kerstin Carlsdotter. He and his wife (2048-344) Elisabeth Håkansdotter Hand is buried in Hössna church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Elisabet Hand,''' to Hössna and Gavlö, born 1598, died 1651-04-10 and buried in Hössna church, daughter of the governor Håkan Hand and Virginia, King Erik XIV's natural daughter with Agda Persdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT *''' Johan Persson''' born 1617. Rider. Death 1688. Johan , (son of Per Joensson, adlad Gyllenswaard), to Sunnaryd and Bolstad (Bolmstad) in Bolmsö parish, Gavlö in Dannäs parish (all in Jönköping County) and Priesttorp in Berga p
2 CONC arish, Kronoberg county. Born 1617-05-13. Be a fan of Småland's riders 1635 2 . Lieutenant there. 1636 2 . Rider champion 1644 2 –1655, from 1646 as reformed. Died 1688-02-02. His coat of arms was erected in Bolmsö old church in S
2 CONC måland and, at the expense of members of the family in 1926, was restored in the restored 1839 church. Married to Märta Stierna , daughter of rider champion Måns Stierna and Anna Siöblad .
2 CONT *''' Knut Persson''' Regimental Quartermaster. Knut , (son of Per Joensson, adlad Gyllenswaard). Be a member of the Jönköping Regiment in 1644 1 . Transp. to Colonel Silfverhielm's regiment 1645 1 . Regiment Quartermaster at the D
2 CONC utch Regiment. Died in 1664 (shortly before 12/4) and buried s. On. In Hössna church Älvsborg county. Married to Eufrosyne Lillie af Aspenäs in her 1st marriage (married 2nd before 1674 to Captain Gustaf Silfverlåås ), daughter of
2 CONC  the Lieutenant Colonel Peder Lillie af Aspenäs , and Maria Amalia von Lepel.
2 CONT *''' Virginia Persdotter,''' lived as a widow in 1685.  Married in 1641 with substitute Johan Gustafsson , left Örnevinge in his 1st wedding, died in 1685.
2 CONT * '''Märta Persdotter,''' to Önnarp, which was reduced to 1689 from her, born 1620, died 1694-11-11 Önnarp Married to Captain Jonas Larsson Silfverswärd , died in 1656.
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000001985522486&photo_id=6000000088841759827&position=8 '''Beata Persdotter'''] Lived widow in 1698. Married to the major Jöns Svinhufvud in Västergötland, (no.199)
2 CONC , born circa 1621 in Önnarp, Hossna, Åsundenleden, Sweden & died on November 11, 1698 in Laxarby, i Steneby (P), Sweden.  
2 CONT
