2 CONC neby, for his lifetime service as her servant and fishermen. Beata died probably on the yard bågenholm during the  winter of 1701-1702 because on 3 February 1701 at Bågeholm they established a testamentsskrift between the Lieutena
2 CONC nt Jöns Johansson Svinehufvud (Beatas grandchildren) and his cousin the Virgin Mary Bullock, wherein the Lieutenant bequeathed half of his unencumbered sätsgård Bogeholm to her, "making himself a free disposition, with the assuran
