1 NOTE In 1560 he became duke of Södermanland, and in 1568 he aided his brother 
2 CONT John III in deposing their older brother Eric XIV.  When John died in 1592 
2 CONT and was succeeded by his son, King Sigismund III of Poland, Charles became 
2 CONT regent for his absent nephew. Charles, a Protestant, aroused the populace 
2 CONT against his nephew, an ardent Roman Catholic. Sigismund landed in Sweden 
2 CONT in 1598 and was defeated by Charles at Stângebro. Sigismund was formally 
2 CONT deposed in 1599, and Charles in 1604 yielded to popular demand and was 
2 CONT crowned king of Sweden. Charles was an ambitious, ruthless, but able 
2 CONT leader, who was unpopular because of his costly wars with Poland, Russia, 
2 CONT and Denmark. He was succeeded by his son Gustav II Adolph.
