1 NAME Jöen /Jönsson i Gavlö/
2 GIVN Jöen
2 SURN Jönsson i Gavlö
2 NICK Gångeskomakare i Västergötland på 1500-talet
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1570
2 ADDR
3 CITY Björnsäter
3 STAE Östergötland
3 CTRY Sweden
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1611
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Denmark
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Jöen Jönsson i Gavlö=
2 CONT
2 CONT Also known as Store-Jon in Svinanäs (Gavlö)
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.roskildehistorie.dk/stamtavler/adel/svenske/F-smaa/Falkenfelt.htm '''Could he be from the Family of Falkenfelt Falkensköld, Falkenclou, Rytterström?'''] It shows a Johan Johansson Falck, who  shows the same sword fr
2 CONC om the Coat of Arms of  Per Joensson Gyllensvard, till Önnarp, who could be the son of Johan (Hans) Eriksson Falck, who is the son of Erik Johansson Falk who was a bishop of i Skara in 1547 and Linköping stift 1558 who was married
2 CONC  to Kerstin Arvidsdotter Store. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Fell in Denmark in 1611
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://forum.rotter.se/index.php?topic=65571.0 Rotters Forum]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sylvia et al, also read Carl-Gösta Gyllenswärd's article Ätten Gyllenswärd - officers and landowners in Sunnerbokrönika 17th century, part 2 (1997) page 61-69. The data in this article, as well as those published by Sölve Olsson i
2 CONC n Dannäs en Västbosocken, must be taken with a pinch of salt, because they combined several different Jon (not Joen, it is only a dialectal writing variant that seems difficult to eradicate among genealogy and homeland researchers
2 CONC , cf. Suen for Sven, Måens for Måns, Jöens for Jöns, etc.) and also constructed several family links back to the sheriff Jon in Gavlö who is mentioned in the middle of the 16th century. It is conjecture and nothing else, so the Wi
2 CONC kipedia article, whoever wrote it, has no source-critical basis to stand on.
2 CONT
2 CONT Store-Jon in Svinanäs (Gavlö) is mentioned in the Västbo dombok in the early 17th century and his full name is Jon Jönsson and he owns Svinanäs (part of Gavlö) and for chronological reasons he cannot be the same as the Jon in Gavl
2 CONC ö who figures in the middle of the 16th century. Per Jonsson Gyllenswärd also has his brother Sven Jonsson Falk (married to Brita Persdotter Lilliehöök who was born of salvation) who lived in Gavlö, also his brother Jöns Jonssons,
2 CONC  bailiff at Toftaholm and resident of Ingelstad in Berga parish (Sunnerbo district) children called Falk. Gavlö is the inheritance land of these brothers and caused a lot of family conflicts in the 17th century which can be traced
2 CONC  in Västbo court records. Also read about this in Almquist Frälsegodsen during the great power era.
2 CONT
2 CONT At present, there is no completely certain information, except that Per Jonsson Gyllenswärd and his brothers had inherited land in Gavlö, which indicates a relationship with Per Jonsson (Gavlösläkten) who held the farm under prote
2 CONC ction in the 1570s - however, the brothers cannot possibly be his grandchildren PJ mentioned in Sunnerbokrönika part 2. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.roskildehistorie.dk/stamtavler/adel/svenske/F-smaa/Falkenfelt.htm
