2 CONT Korsbyn 1 qvarn., Lund 1 d:o. Sannerud 1 d:o.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Manor. (Boifuen.) 3)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Belonged to the presbytery in Skara in 1480. according to its land register. See the attachment.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Called Shows.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Egdes 1563 by wife Karin at Dingelvik: 1577 by Nils Månsson at Bro; 1619 by wife Margreta to Bro: 1637 by Carl Svinhufvud at Dingelvik; In 1664 it was Jöns Svinhufvud's manor house: in 1681 by wife Beata Gyllensvärd, then calle
2 CONC d Bågenholm and referred to as old manor house. Owned until 1790 by the contract provost, doctor Anders Sörström in Hesselskog: 1795 by his widow 1809 by Carl Fr. OWL; 1850 by Anders Olsson in Grättved.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) Obey the Billingsfors community.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The hanger. Manor.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Ivägsholm. (Wageln.) 3)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Called Arnlingen.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Some of this is called Gillerud. b ti Swedish Diplomatarium No. 1686, during the 6 July 1310. a letter of confirmation of Bishop Bruiolfs in Skara on the Inte domprosten Bengt made by the homeman of Hesselskog's church, among w
2 CONC hich a örtugsbol in A vangen. by which is probably meant a part in this home. 1 Wadstena monastery's land register (see appendix) is named Wonginne as it is located near Va-ttinghurn.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Owned in 1664 by the well-born Patrik Thomson: in 1681 by Göran Svenske and then called the old manor. Received the name Ivägsholm in 1687. Owned in 1691 by the lieutenant Jöns Johansson Svinhufvud. In 1698 he sold the manor to
2 CONC  the well-born Filip Konrad Blom for 600 r:dr curant at 6 marks each, d. eh. according to the current im calculation approximately 1,200 r:dr b:ko. In 1783, contract provost Lars Wallstedt in Steneln was the owner. In 1822 his suc
2 CONC cessor, contract provost Carl Gust. Schroeder. whose widow Britta Collin bequeathed the homestead to the 3 sons of the parish priest in Steneby Per Johan Lundberg, who are now the owners. since the death of the dowager in 1842. IV
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=
2 CONT
2 CONT Jöns Carlsson Svinhufvud and Beata Gyllensvärd, "Vasatös" was held in April 1645 long Jöns. AREDS Sconce at Jönköping. Om it was there he met his future wife, I don't know, but (in the Lucia days) on 13 December 1646 marries Jöns 
2 CONC Carlsson Svinhufvud with Beata Gyllensvärd in Åsundenleden. In the morning his wife gave a gift to Jons Carlsson Svinhufvud, the deed reads in brief summary: ' Hs.Kl.M:st My Allernådigaste to the Swedish Queen & Faith and tiänare 
2 CONC and öffuer lldige Fendrich – itt Compagnie Närkes and Wermlands Infanterie Jagh Jöns Svinehufet to Dijnevijk and Bouent. For everyone that this bref förekänt hermedh giör, vetterligit happens, that when iagh and frelsares sextonhu
2 CONC ndrade our fyrattyosex after Byrd's denn 13 Project. Through his Höges Gracious försyhn, sampt pare these was slecht hölt venners and consent and Bröloph on Åsundenleden, medh denn Edla and Velb.Virgo Beata Gyldensuerdh Adeliga an
2 CONC d Gudsfruchtiga persons in the present tense and närevaron, who were present, "hath iagh after fadherehnligh and plägsedh gifuet utlofvat and Adelig bestowed such as and now, on the right and this time force are just some of the i
2 CONC mpediments to gifuer Velborna my iämpte skyldigh huusfru K kiärligh: sämia faithful to honorable and Morgongåfua Bouent in Uedboo häradh and Laxaboo halfparten located in the parish and loose and fast and it also owns and hafuer i
2 CONC agh förvärft and ärfva förevärfa hereafter, and can and to förbättringh hafuer iagh gifuet Ducater her four hundredth " As guarantors of the morning gift was signed the document of the siblings of the bride but also by senior mili
2 CONC tary officers in the family. His wife Beata Gyllensvärd was probably born at the family estate Önnarp in Åsundenleden in early 1620 's. Her father was a Parliamentarian Per Jonsson Gyllensvärd, mother Elisabeth Håkansdotter Hand. 
2 CONC Per Jonsson Gyllensvärd and Elisabeth Håkansdotter
2 CONT
