1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Maria Catharina Jonsdotter Svinhufvud pa Lilla Dufhult=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Jöns Svinhufvud (- 1659) &  Beata Gyllensvärd, 
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003897396711&photo_id=6000000089040702855&position=1 '''Daughter of Major Jöns Carlsson Svinhufvud and Beata Persdotter Gyllensvärd''']
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000003897396711?album_type=photos_of_me&end=&photo_id=6000000080782028955&project_id=&start=&tagged_profiles= '''Birth Record:''' April 11, 1649 in i Röksberg, Mulseryd förs, Jönköpings län (
2 CONC F), Sverige (Sweden)] 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003897396711&photo_id=6000000201915681825&position=0 '''Medieval stained glass with the boar's head coat of arms in Torsång's church, Dalarna, now in the Histori
2 CONC cal Museum, Stockholm. Photo: Riksantikvarieämbetet''']
2 CONT *'''Donations in Västervik, Femsjö and tax exemption in Önnarp'''. - In a letter from 7 October 1620 it appears that Per Jonsson had been promoted to lieutenant and that he received a farm in Västervik as a donation. In 1624 he re
2 CONC ceived the Yaböke estate and the Gullnubb croft in Femsjö parish as a donation (the Yaböke estate would later be taken over by his granddaughter Maria Catharina Svinhufvud and Johan Carl Rosenschantz). Per had risen further in the
2 CONC  ranks, now he was a captain. On 3 March 1629 he received in a letter from Gustav II Adolf, tax exemption on a tax home in Önnarp, as well as on his own tax farm in Hössna in Västergötland, as well as on four crofts, Hallen, Hästh
2 CONC agen and Höghult in Hössna and Tuskan in Liared parish in Redvägs district in Västergötland. According to one source, Per had purchased Hössna a few years earlier. Another source claims that it came through the marriage to Elisabe
2 CONC th, which I think is most likely. Per was now promoted to Ryttmästare. 
2 CONT *  [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003897396711&photo_id=6000000080782028955&position=2 '''Death Record:''' 1720-02-11 Femsjö, Halland, Maria Catharina Svinhufvud Lived 70 years]
2 CONT * Buried: on 1720-02-28 in i Femsjö Kirkegaard, Femsjö, Halland, Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Maria Catharina Svinhufvud's Original Death Record: February 11, 1720 (70) Lilla Duvhult, Femsjö, Halland, Sweden=
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000080782028955&size=large}}
2 CONT '''Death Record Translated into English:'''  On February 11th, the Matron Lady Maria Catharina Svinhufvud died in Lilla Duvhult, was born at Solberga in Mo härad [District] Anno 1649. On April 11th married to the late Sir  Johan C
2 CONC arl Rosenschantz, in true [matrimony] 1666 on August 21st until the year 1713 in May, which was 47 years; lived as a widow since for nearly 7 years. Her entire age was 70 years 10 months, was buried alongside her late lord and hus
2 CONC band in Femsiö Kyrkiogård, d. 28 Febr. anno 1720."sjö Churchyard, on February 28th, in the year 1720.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003897396711&photo_id=6000000089040702855&position=1 ''' Johan Carl Rosenschantz'''] on August 21,1666 in Mulseryd Jönköping, Sverige, located in northe
2 CONC rn Småland. Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Rosenschantz_nr_570 '''Genealogy of the Rosenschantz, Tab 2'''] 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children of Johan Carl Rosenschantz and Maria Catharina Svinhufvud=
2 CONT
2 CONT *(1)''''''' Beata''''''' -  Married 1690-10-04 with korpralen Knut Andersson Svan in Yaböke (in Femsjö socken).
2 CONT
2 CONT *(2)''''''' Johan Georg'''''''-  Lieutenant. Death 1719. Musketeer in the German Life Regiment of Foot 1699. Master of the Guard in the German Life Regiment of Foot 1700. Sergeant 1700. Ensign 1704-03-04. Lieutenant 1711-03-27. Co
2 CONC nfirmation power 1715-02-08. Died 1719 in Norway, leaving behind an only daughter. Married 1704-04-26 in Karlskrona to Anna Regina Tharmoth , born 1680, died 1762-11-12 in Stockholm, daughter of Major Jakob Tharmoth, ennobled Thar
2 CONC moth , and his 3rd wife Barbara von Schmiegelin.
2 CONT
2 CONT *(3)''''''' Märta'''''''-  Married 1710-03-27 with Korpralen Bengt Jonsson in Frillalt (in the Femsjö parish).
2 CONT
2 CONT *(4)''''''' Christina'''''''- Married 1711-05-17 with boy Bengt Andersson from Eskilsbo in Torup parish, Halland County.
2 CONT
2 CONT *(5)''''''' Anna Rosina'''''''- born 1680, died 1762-11-00 in Stockholm. Married to the private E. Westh.
2 CONT
2 CONT *(6)''''''' Catharina''''''' - born 1688, died 1773-11-20 in Gränna and in Gränna buried 1773-11-30. Married to the country fisherman Rafael Björkengren , born 1693, dead 1750-01-06 in Gränna.
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Maria Chatarina Svinhufvud''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Maria Chatarina Svinhufvud", was the wife of Johan Carl Rosenschantz, she was born at Mulseryd farm in the parish of Röksberg seated in Northern Småland on 11 April 1649. In 1688, she stood as taxpayers to the Church and after he
2 CONC r husband's death, lived on the farm at Lilla Duvhult until her death at the age of almost 71 on 11 February 1720.  She was buried, "alongside their Sal Lord and husband at Femsjö cemetery". Maria Chatarina heard enough to calm am
2 CONC ong Svinhufvudena. Her parents were, Captain Jöns Svinhufvud and Beata Gyllensvärd, who is the great grandaugher of Erik XIV King of Sweden and Agda “Charitas” Persdotter.  Maria’s Svinhufvud’s father Jöns Svinhufvud was born in t
2 CONC he parish of Brill, Dalsland in 1622. His father was Major Carl J Svinhufvud and mother Margareta Lennartsdotter Svenske. Already as a 14 year old boy when his father became fatherless Jöns was killed in Svinhufvud Verb in Saxony,
2 CONC  Germany on September 1636. In patrimony, he received the yards Your gel Bay and Bow in Dalsland with associated small farms. Jöns also in the military,  received the rank of captain in 1656 Närkes Värmlands regemente. During the 
2 CONC thirty years ' war he was a second lieutenant and Lieutenant in different companies of the regiment and participated in ilmarschen, Germany to Jutland 1643-1644. He also participated in the Charles X war against Poland and Russia 
2 CONC and was present on the daring March across the Belt on the night of 11 February 1659, he was also present at the storming of Copenhagen when he was hit by a muskötkula and died of the injury on June 17 between the hours of 11 and 
2 CONC 12 at night in field camp in Bromshög on the island of Zealand Denmark. He received his final resting place in the cemetery of Mulseryd, which is supported by the cash gifts listed in the Church accounts in Mulseryds kyrkobok: "An
2 CONC no 1660 Theff. Efterskrefne have been given to the Church. Velb.Peder J on Jan 5 Rijd. And promise us that with give 5 der.Huilket became League  then s. Mann Hr Jöns Svinehufvd to Rögberg promised 10 Rijd.5 af them hava velb. Wif
2 CONC e nedhlag and 5 lovfa she vylija with the last "alra.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jöns Carlsson Svinhufvud and Beata Gyllensvärd, "Vasatös" was held in april 1645 long Jöns.  AREDS Sconce at Jönköping. Om it was there he met his future wife, I don't know, but (in the Lucia days) on 13 December 1646 marries Jöns
2 CONC   Carlsson Svinhufvud with Beata Gyllensvärd in Åsundenleden.  In the morning his wife gave a gift to Jons Carlsson Svinhufvud, the deed reads in brief summary: ' Hs.Kl.M:st  My Allernådigaste to the Swedish Queen & Faith and tiän
2 CONC are and öffuer lldige Fendrich – itt Compagnie Närkes and Wermlands Infanterie Jagh Jöns Svinehufet to Dijnevijk and Bouent. For everyone that this bref förekänt hermedh giör, vetterligit happens, that when iagh and frelsares sext
2 CONC onhundrade our fyrattyosex after Byrd's denn 13 Project. Through his Höges Gracious försyhn, sampt pare these was slecht hölt venners and consent and Bröloph on Åsundenleden, medh denn Edla and Velb.Virgo Beata Gyldensuerdh Adelig
2 CONC a and Gudsfruchtiga persons in the present tense and närevaron, who were present, "hath iagh after fadherehnligh and plägsedh gifuet utlofvat and Adelig bestowed such as and now, on the right and this time force are just some of t
2 CONC he impediments to gifuer Velborna my iämpte skyldigh huusfru K kiärligh: sämia faithful to honorable and Morgongåfua Bouent in Uedboo häradh and Laxaboo halfparten located in the parish and loose and fast and it also owns and hafu
2 CONC er iagh förvärft and ärfva förevärfa herefter, and can and to förbättringh hafuer iagh gifuet Ducater her four hundredth " As guarantors of the morning gift was signed the document of the siblings of the bride but also by senior m
2 CONC ilitary officers in the family. His wife Beata Gyllensvärd was probably born at the family estate Önnarp in Åsundenleden in early 1620 's. His father was a Parliamentarian Per Jonsson Gyllensvärd, mother Elisabeth Håkansdotter Han
2 CONC d. Per Jonsson Gyllensvärd and Elisabeth Håkansdotter.
2 CONT
