1 NAME Berend Johann /von Schulmann/
2 GIVN Berend Johann
2 _MARNM von Schulmann
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC St Nicholas' Church
2 ADDR
3 CITY Tallinn
3 STAE Harju
3 CTRY Estonia
1 BIRT
2 DATE 2 FEB 1660
1 DEAT
2 DATE 29 SEP 1746
2 ADDR
3 CITY Reval
3 CTRY Estonia
1 OCCU Major, lantråd
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wiki: [ http://et.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berend_Johann_von_Schulmann]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://personen.digitale-sammlungen.de/baltlex/Blatt_bsb00000600,00278.html?prozent=
2 CONT
2 CONT VII.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Släkten Schulman-von Schulmann i Sverige, Finland och Baltikum
2 CONT Tammerfors 1938-Tammerfors Handelstryckeri
2 CONT https://asiakkaamme.fi/schulmans/index.html#p=276
2 CONT
2 CONT He joined the Castle Watch in Reval on November 24th 1685.
2 CONT
2 CONT In August 1687 he was in a duel with officer candidate von Dannenfeld.   Von Dannenfeld publicly accused him of not being worth of his position.  He said to a third party in the main square of Reval that Berendt's success was only
2 CONC  due to his parents.  If he was an officer candidate at such an early age he knew nothing of the world.
2 CONT
2 CONT The results of the duel are unknown but the duel did lead to an issue being raised if to members of the nobility in public service, one with the city and the other with the garrison should be allowed to settle a dispute through a 
2 CONC duel.  
2 CONT
2 CONT March 25th 1693 he became Manngerichtsassessor.
2 CONT
2 CONT From October 17th 1697 till into 1698 he was in Stockholm as a representative of the aristocracy from Estonia.
2 CONT
2 CONT December 12th 1699 he was elected into the Ritterschaftlichen Asschuss.
2 CONT
2 CONT Starting on July 8th 1708 he was in the Landtag in Reval.
2 CONT
2 CONT On February 1st 1711 under the new Russian authority he was the first mannrichter appointed in Wierland and Jerwen.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Great Northern War and the plague of 1710 left Estonia with very few members of the nobility.   In December 1711 there were only 312 members of the nobility in Estonia of which 116 were children.   Berendt was the only adult m
2 CONC ale Schulmann in Estonia at the time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Berendt was first proposed as Ritterschaftshautpmann in 1711.  He was not chosen in that year but was selected in the next term in 1713.
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited the estates Hackeweide, Sall, Koil, and Moisamaa.  He later purchased Poeddrang in Kirchspeil St. Marien and Tammik.  Tammik was purchased from Wolmar Heinrich von Brummer.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the time of his death he owned five estates without debts, he 11,000 Reichstaler in cash,   In his will he freed his servants and gave 300 reichstaler.   His will also gave 200 reichstaler to the Nikolai Church and Dom Church i
2 CONC n Reval, and other 200 to each of the schools connected the chruches and 200 to St Simonis church, Maria-Magdalenen chuch, the hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried in the Nikolai Church in the family vault under stone #13.  The church has on the wall a Schulmann crest because of his donation to the chuch
2 CONT
2 CONT At the death of his father-in-law he also managed of Fickel, Menzen, and Gross Sauss
