1 NOTE {geni:about_me} = Dorothea von Brandenburg=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Frederick II Hohenzollern, Elector and Katherina von Sachsen, Kurfürstin zu Brandenburg 
2 CONT * Dorothea of Brandenburg (1446 – March 1519) was a princess of Brandenburg by birth and by marriage Duchess of Saxe-Lauenburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXONY.htm#BernhardIILauenburgdied1463A Project MedLands Saxony Dukes]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BERNHARD von Sachsen-Lauenburg, son of ERICH IV Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg & his wife Sophie von Braunschweig''' (-16 Jul 1463, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Bernd”, who inherit
2 CONC ed “de Herschopp to Louenborch”, third of the three sons of “Hertoghe Ereke to Sassen, ein Her to Louenborch” and his wife[694].  He succeeded his brother in 1435 as BERNHARD II Herzog von Sachsen in Lauenburg und Ratzeburg.  '''m
2 CONC arried  (2 Feb 1429) ADELHEID von Pommern, daughter of BOGISLAW VIII Duke of Pomerania in Hinterpommern & his wife Sophie von Holstein ([1410]-after 1445).'''  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum records that “Hertoghe Ber
2 CONC nd, Hertoghen Ereken sone to Sassen, unde eyn Here to Louenborch” married “Alheys, des Hertoghen dochter to Pomeren in der Slesye”[695]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bernhard von Sachsen-Lauenburg & his wife ADELHEID von Pommern had two children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''JOHANN von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (18 Jul 1439-15 Aug 1507, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Johanns”, who succeeded his father, as the son of “Hertoghe Bernd, Hertoghen E
2 CONC reken sone to Sassen, unde eyn Here to Louenborch” and his wife[696].  He succeeded his father in 1463 as JOHANN V Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg.  '''married  (Lüneburg 12 Feb 1464) DOROTHEA von Brandenburg, daughter of FRIEDRICH I
2 CONC I Markgraf and Elector of Brandenburg & his wife Katharina von Sachsen (1446-1519 before 20 Mar, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral).'''  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Dorothea”, who married “Hertoghen Hans te Loenborch”
2 CONC , second of the two daughters of “Marggreve Frederick de elder, Marggreve Frederikes sone to Brandenborch” and his wife[697].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johann & his wife DOROTHEA von Brandenburg had thirteen children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>* a)        ''' ERICH von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-20 Oct 1522).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Erekes” first among the seven sons of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen under so Louenborch” and 
2 CONC his wife[698].  Canon at Köln Cathedral 1490.  Canon at Hildesheim Cathedral 1492.  Elected Bishop of Hildesheim 1503/1504.  Bishop of Münster 1508.
2 CONT >>>* b)         '''MAGNUS von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-1 Aug 1543, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Magnus” second among the seven sons of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen
2 CONC  under so Louenborch” and his wife[699].  He succeeded his father in 1507 as MAGNUS I Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg. 
2 CONT >>>* c)         '''BERNHARD von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-3 Jan 1524).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Bernd” third among the seven sons of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen under so Louenborch” and
2 CONC  his wife[700].  Provost at Münster Cathedral 1510.  Canon and provost at Köln, St Gereon 1512.
2 CONT >>>* d)         '''JOHANN von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-20 Nov 1547).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Hans” fourth among the seven sons of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen under so Louenborch” and 
2 CONC his wife[701].  Bishop of Hildesheim 1504, resigned 1527.   
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johann had two illegitimate children by unknown mistresses:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* i)          '''JOHANN von Sachsen''' .  A priest in Berkenthin, near Ratzeburg 1538.
2 CONT >>>>>* ii)         '''BERNHARD von Sachsen''' ([1530-Livonia [1592/1612]).  He served in the Swedish army.  '''married firstly (before 1555) ---''' (-1590).  '''married secondly (before 1591) DOROTHEA von Lewald, daughter of JOHAN
2 CONC N von Lewald [Liebenrode] zu Malla & his wife Magdalene von Rosen a.d.H. Hochrosen.'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bernhard von Sachsen & his unknown first wife had three children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>* (a)        '''GIESELA von Sachsen'''  She was known as "die schöne Buhlerin/the beautiful prostitute"[702].  '''married  (1575) ADAM von Tschammer,''' son of ---.  Counsellor of the duchy of Sachsen-Lauenburg 1593.  Mistr
2 CONC ess of: her cousin, MORITZ Herzog zu Sachsen-Lauenburg, son of FRANZ I Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg & his wife Sibylla von Sachsen (1551-Buxtehude 2 Nov 1612, bur Ratzeburg). 
2 CONT >>>>>>>* (b)        '''daughter''' 1581/1615.  married KONRAD von Sondershausen, son of ---.  Counsellor of the duchy of Sachsen Lauenburg 1575/1581. 
2 CONT >>>>>>>* (c)        '''SIBYLLE''' ([1560]-after 1615).  m (Buxtehude 2 Jul 1593) EMEKE von Roeder zu Grönholt, son of ---.  1582/1593.
2 CONT >>>>>* e)         '''RUDOLF von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-1503, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Roleff” fifth among the seven sons of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen unde
2 CONC r so Louenborch” and his wife[703]. 
2 CONT >>>>>* f)          '''HEINRICH von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-young).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Hinrick” who died young sixth among the seven sons of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen under so 
2 CONC Louenborch” and his wife[704]. 
2 CONT >>>>>* g)         '''FRIEDRICH von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-before 1501).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Frederick” who died young seventh among the seven sons of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen
2 CONC  under so Louenborch” and his wife[705]. 
2 CONT >>>>>* h)         '''ADELHEID von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-young).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Aleys” who died young eldest of the six daughters of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen under so Lo
2 CONC uenborch” and his wife[706]. 
2 CONT >>>>>* i)         ''' KATHARINA von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' .  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Katerina”, a nun, second of the six daughters of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen under so Louenborch” 
2 CONC and his wife[707].  A nun in Reinbek.
2 CONT >>>>>* j)          '''ELISABETH von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-after 7 Apr 1542[708]).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Elizabeth” third of the six daughters of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen under
2 CONC  so Louenborch” and his wife[709].  '''married  (Einbeck 26 Aug 1494) HEINRICH IV Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen,''' son of HEINRICH III Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen & his wife Margareta von Sagan [Piast] ([1460]-Salzd
2 CONC erhelden 6 Dec 1526).
2 CONT >>>>>* k)         '''SOPHIE von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-before 1497, bur Obernkirchen).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Soffya” fourth of the six daughters of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen und
2 CONC er so Louenborch” and his wife[710].  '''married  (29 Nov 1492) as his first wife, ANTONIUS Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg,''' son of OTTO II Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg & his wife Elisabeth von Honstein ([1439]-22 Dec 1526, bur 
2 CONC Obernkirchen).  He succeeded his brother in 1498 as Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg in Rodenberg und Schaumburg. 
2 CONT >>>>>* l)          '''ANNA von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-Burg Ohsen 9 Aug 1504, bur Marienau).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Anna”, who married “Greve Hans to Reppyn”, fifth of the six daughters of “Hertoghe Han
2 CONC s, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen under so Louenborch” and his wife[711].  '''married firstly (early 1490) JOHANN III Graf von Lindau-Ruppin,''' son of --- (-14 Jun 1500).  '''married secondly (contract 25 Jun 1503) FRIEDRICH Gr
2 CONC af von Spiegelberg in Spiegelberg und Pyrmont,'''son of --- (-Pyrmont 5 Mar 1537, bur Marienau). 
2 CONT >>>>>* m)       '''MARGARETA von Sachsen-'''Lauenburg''' (-young).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Margareta” who died “ein junckfruwe” sixth of the six daughters of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sa
2 CONC ssen under so Louenborch” and his wife[712]. 
2 CONT * 2.         '''SOPHIE von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-9 Sep 1473).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Soffya”, who married “den Hertoghen van den Barge”, as daughter of “Hertoghe Bernd, Hertoghen Ereken sone to Sassen
2 CONC , unde eyn Here to Louenborch” and his wife[713].  The Memorienbuch of Düsseldorf St Maria records the death "VI Id Sep 1473" of "domine Sophie de Sassen ducisse Juliacensis et Montensis" and in memorial of “domini Gerardi ducis e
2 CONC ius conthoralis”[714].  '''married (1444) GERHARD VII Duke of Jülich and Berg''' son of WILHELM von Jülich Graf von Ravensberg & his wife Adelheid von Tecklenburg (-18 Aug 1475).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dorothea_of_Brandenburg,_Duchess_of_Saxe-Lauenburg Dorothea of Brandenburg, Duchess of Saxe-Lauenburg, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothea was the eldest child of Elector Frederick II of Brandenburg (1413–1471) from his marriage to Catherine (1421–1476), daughter of Elector Frederick I of Saxony.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married on 12 February 1464 in Lüneburg Duke John V of Saxe-Lauenburg (1439–1507). As she was oldest daughter of the Elector Frederick, who had no surviving sons, the marriage agreement was important. In addition to a 10000 fl
2 CONC orins dowry, Frederick promised his son-in-law everything that he could legally leave to his daughter. Later, however, Frederick abdicated in favour of his younger brother Albert Achilles, so as to keep his possessions in the fami
2 CONC ly.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick also failed to pay the dowry to his son-in-law. This led Dorothea's uncle John the Alchemist to compare himself with the Elector Frederick in 1482
2 CONT
