1 OCCU Duke of Mecklenburg-Schwerin, married May 14, 1551
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry V, Duke of Mecklenburg, nicknamed the Peaceful (3 May 1479 – 6 February 1552), was the reigning Duke of Mecklenburg in the region Mecklenburg-Schwerin, the son of Duke Magnus II and Sophie of Pomerania-Stetti
2 CONC n.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry ruled jointly with his brothers Eric II and Albert VII and his uncle Balthasar from 27 December 1503. Balthasar died on 16 March 1507 and Eric on 22 December 1508, both without an heir, thus Henry and Albert came into posses
2 CONC sion of the whole country. They ruled jointly at first. Albert repeatedly advocated the division of the territories of Mecklenburg, and this was agreed to in the House Treaty of Neubrandenburg, sealed on 7 May 1520. The treaty sti
2 CONC pulated that Henry rule in Schwerin and Albert in Güstrow, without a de facto division of the country.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was during the reign of the brothers Henry and Albert that Martin Luther launched the Reformation, which quickly found supporters in Mecklenburg. Lutheran doctrine was preached there more or less openly as early as 1523 and per
2 CONC haps even earlier. Duke Henry supported the new doctrine from the beginning, at first in a very cautious manner, and but more openly after the Diet of Augsburg in 1530. He corresponded with Luther beginning in 1524, and Luther sen
2 CONC t him teachers and preachers.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT *[http://thepeerage.com/p11137.htm#i111364 The peerage]
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/D/per_page.php?id=2376 Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_V,_Duke_of_Mecklenburg Wikipedia] 	
2 CONT *'''Duke of Mecklenburg:''' Reign 1503–1520, with [http://www.geni.com/people/Albrecht-VII-von-Mecklenburg/6000000003858766329 Albert VII](brother) (1503–1520), [http://www.geni.com/people/Erich-II-von-Mecklenburg/6000000006727778
2 CONC 798 Eric II] (brother) (1503–1508) and [http://www.geni.com/people/Balthasar-von-Mecklenburg/6000000006727790651 Balthasar] (uncle) (1479–1507)
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Balthasar-von-Mecklenburg/6000000006727790651 Balthasar] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Magnus-II-von-Mecklenburg/6000000007606027348 Magnus II] of Mecklenburg '''Successor:''' [htt
2 CONC p://www.geni.com/people/Albrecht-VII-von-Mecklenburg/6000000003858766329 Albert VII] of Mecklenburg-Güstrow [http://www.geni.com/people/Heinrich-V-Herzog-von-Mecklenburg-Schwerin/6000000006727778773 Henry V] as Duke of Mecklenburg
2 CONC -Schwerin	
2 CONT *'''Duke of Mecklenburg-Schwerin: Reign 1520–1552
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Albrecht-VII-von-Mecklenburg/6000000003858766329 Albert VII] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Heinrich-V-Herzog-von-Mecklenburg-Schwerin/6000000006727778773 Henry V] as Dukes of Meckl
2 CONC enburg '''Successor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Johann-Albrecht-I-Herzog-von-Mecklenburg-G%C3%BCstrow-Schwerin/6000000006727749566 John Albert I] of Mecklenburg-Schwerin
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Mecklenburg-29]
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry V, Duke of Mecklenburg, nicknamed the Peaceful, (3 May 1479 – 6 February 1552) was the reigning Duke of Mecklenburg in the region Mecklenburg-Schwerin, the son of Duke Magnus II and Sophie of Pomerania-Stettin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was married three times.
2 CONT
2 CONT He first married Ursula of Brandenburg (17 October 1488 – 18 September 1510), daughter of the elector John II Cicero of Brandenburg, on 12 December 1505. They had three children together:
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus (1509–1550), Duke of Mecklenburg-Schwerin, Administrator of the Prince-Bishopric of Schwerin, and from 1532 Bishop of Schwerin.
2 CONT Sophie (1508–1541), who married Duke Ernest of Brunswick-Lüneburg. Ursula († 1586), last abbess of the Poor Clares monastery at Ribnitz. Henry's second marriage, on 12 June 1513, was to Helen of the Palatinate (1493 – 4 August 152
2 CONC 4), daughter of Philipp, Elector Palatine. They also had three children together:
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip (1514–1557), Duke of Mecklenburg-Schwerin Margaret (d. 1586), who married Duke Henry II, Duke of Münsterberg-Oels. Catherine (d. 1586), who married Frederick III, Duke of Legnica. His third marriage (concluded on 14 May 155
2 CONC 1) was to Ursula (died after 1565), daughter of Magnus I, Duke of Saxe-Lauenburg, and his wife Catherine of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel, Duchess of Saxe-Lauenburg. This marriage was childless.
