1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1674 he was made Knight of the Danebrog and appointed Field Marshal by King Christian V of Denmark to command the Danish army in a joint offensive (with Brandenburg) against Sweden. The army of 18,000 men and fo
2 CONC rty guns set off  through neutral Mecklenburg in September 1675. They took Wismar on 20 September and then took Doberan on 25th. Damgarten was taken on 6 October. Weiher is possibly portrayed on the Rosenborg tapestries.
