1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Wikipedia==  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Baron''' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Klas_Horn '''Klas Kristersson Horn'''] was a Finnish-born Swedish nobleman and naval admiral who fought for Sweden in the Northern Seven Years' War of 1563–1570.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horn_family '''Horn'''] '''was born''' at Åminne Manor in Halikko, Finland. He was the son of Krister Klasson Horn and Ingeborg Siggesdotter Sparre. He received his early education in the court of 
2 CONC Philip I, Duke of Pomerania. In 1550, King Gustav I of Sweden made him the head of the district of southern Finland at Raseborg.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He participated''' in the expeditions of Jakob Bagge during the fall of 1555. In 1556, he was sent to Viborg Castle and the following year was made commander. In 1559, he won a number of battles against Danish naval forces unde
2 CONC r Herluf Trolle and the Free City of Lübeck. Horn was sent to Reval (now Tallinn) by King Eric XIV of Sweden in March 1561. By June, Toompea Castle was conquered by his troops and Reval became a dominion of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Klas Horn''' was raised to nobility (Horn af Åminne) and made a baron in June 1561. After Jakob Bagge was captured, Klas was promoted to admiral in the Royal Swedish Navy in the fall of 1564. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In January 1565,''' forces under his command sacked the Danish provinces of Scania and Halland. He won a decisive victory over the Danish navy at Bornholm on July 7, 1565 and on July 26, 1566 in the third battle of the northern
2 CONC  part of Öland. He died shortly after being called to command Swedish land forces.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Personal life===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1551, he''' married '''Kerstin Krumme''' (1532–1611). He died at Stora Åby parish in Östergötland, Sweden and was buried at Uppsala Cathedral.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Legacy===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Baron Klas Horn af Åminne''' has been recognized as a naval hero, with both the Royal Swedish Navy and Finnish Navy naming vessels in his honor: HSwMS Klas Horn (1929) and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnish_gunboat_Klas_Hor
2 CONC n Klas Horn] (1892).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Adelsvapen==
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Horn_af_%C3%85minne_nr_2 '''Claes Kristersson Horn den äldre''', ''friherre'' '''Horn af Åminne, till Åminne'''] i Halikko socken i Åbo län, Mustiala i Tammela socken i Tavastland och Skällnor
2 CONC a i Fresta socken Stockholms län. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Född''' omkr. 1518. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Page hos''' hertig Filip I i Pommern. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hovjunkare''' hos konung Gustaf I. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Förseglade''' bland adeln Västerås arvsförening 1544. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Häradshövding''' i Raseborgslän 1550. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Förordnad''' 1554-12-12, att med sin farbror Henrik Klasson Horn föra befälet över krigsfolket i Finland. Följde 1555 fältöversten Jakob Bagge på hans tåg till Nöteborg. Fältöverste vid fotfolket s. å. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ståthållare''' på Viborg 1556 med förnyad fullm. 1557. Fick 1556 i förläning Nurmis gård i Viborgs socken. Avsked 1560. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Beseglade''' konung Gustaf I:s testamente s. å. Deltog i rådsmötet i Arboga 1561. Befallningsman på Reval s. å. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Friherre''' af Åminne 1561-06-29 vid konung Erik XIV:s kröning. Fick s. d. Skällnora gård jämte fem underlydande klostergods i förläning. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Fältherre''' i Livland s. å. Riddare av S:t Salvators eller Guds Lams orden 1562. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Fick s. å. tre''' fjärdingar av Portas socken samt hela Saaris socken och Mustiala gård (allt i Tavastland) som livstids besittning. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Riksråd och''' konung Erik XIV:s sekreteråd 1563. Innehade från s. å. till sin död som förläning Salo bol i Halikko socken (vilket hans änka fick behålla till 1600) och bekom s. å. Sairiala kungsgård i Tavastland som evärdlig e
2 CONC gendom samt s. å. Lindenhof i Estland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Överste för''' det småländska krigsfolket s. å. Överste för allt krigsfolket, både ryttare och knektar i Småland 1564. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Amiral över''' hela k. m:ts flotta s. å. Fältöverste 1565. Amiral på flottan mot Danmark s. å. Amiral över hela konungens skeppsflotta 1566. Överste fältmarskalk s. å. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Död av pesten''' 1566-09-09 s. å. i Åby prästgård i Östergötland och ligger jämte sin fru begraven i S:t Annakoret i Uppsala domkyrka. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Han var en stor hjälte och härförare, så till sjös som lands, reste 1561 till Livland för att av härmästaren Gotthard Kettler fordra ersättning för kaperier å svenska skepp, men då därå ej erhölls nöjaktigt svar, övertalade han i
2 CONC nvånarna i Reval jämte adeln i Harrien, Wierland och Jerven att giva sig under Sverige."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1551-01-03''' Åkerö med Kerstin Krumme, begraven 1611-03-10 i Uppsala domkyrka, dotter av Jakob Nilsson Krumme, till Åkerö och Örboholm, och Anna Clemensdotter Hogenskild. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://runeberg.org/faderhist/0166.html
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.nad.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=13829
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.historiesajten.se/visainfo.asp?id=256
2 CONT
2 CONT http://runeberg.org/frfinl/0200.html
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Klas Kristersson Horn was a Swedish admiral of Finnish origin. He was born around 1517 in Åminne . He participated in the Seven Years War between Denmark and Sweden 1563 - 1570 , where he won a decisive victory over the Danish fle
2 CONC et on July 7 1565 and July 26 1566 , he won over a combined Danish-lübecksk fleet near Öland . He died on September 9 of that year the plague . Married (1551-01-03) by Kerstin Krumme (1532-1611). 
2 CONT
2 CONT He Klas Horn was the son of the centurion and the steward at the Turku Castle in Finland Krister Klasson (Horn) , Sr. to Åminne and Ingeborg Sigge Daughter Sparre . He was probably born on the family farm Åminne . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Early career in the East 
2 CONT
2 CONT His early schooling was Klas Horn page of Duke Philip I of Pomerania and then as hovjunkare of the Swedish king Gustav Vasa . 1550 he became a district judge for southern Finland and Raseborg County. During the Great Russian War ,
2 CONC  he was appointed in 1555 by King Gustav Vasa to the commanders of the army and followed the fall of that year with James Bagge on his train to Noteborg. In 1556 he became one of the governors of Vyborg and the year after the comm
2 CONC ander in Vyborg. In this post he was to become acquainted with the Estonian situation and became in 1560 a Swedish envoy in that country. In 1561 he was sent by King Eric XIV of Reval (now Tallinn), where he persuaded the city's r
2 CONC esidents and nobility of the provinces Harrien and Wierland in June conform in Sweden. The same year he was mentioned as King Eric "rådsförvandt" and received the king's coronation that year baronial dignity. After having laid the
2 CONC  foundation of the Swedish empire south of the Gulf of Finland , he continued in the near future to successfully promote its enlargement. 1561 advising him to advise the newly appointed governor of Reval Lars Fleming. In 1562 Esto
2 CONC nia was separated military and civilian administration, and Klas Horn took over the military command. The same year he conquered PADI and Wittenstein . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nordic Seven Years War  
2 CONT
2 CONT Later in 1562 he returned to Sweden and began the last and most successful period in his life. In the Nordic Seven Years War (1563-70), he had constantly missions both the Army and Navy. After 1563 it participated in the less succ
2 CONC essful campaign against Halmstad he made ​​in February 1564, together with Gustaf Olofsson (Capricorn), an unsuccessful attempt to invade Bohus . Although he was severely reproached by the king, yet he was sent first to the Charle
2 CONC ston County to take command of our forces there, and then, August 8, 1564, he was appointed admiral. After a successful battle against the Danes and Lybeck are at the northern tip of Öland , he was called back to the army and burn
2 CONC ed, after the conquest of Ronneby, (along with Mornay ) Sölvesborg and Elleholm. Barely back from this, he returned for a short time in September admiral of that, back in January 1565 to be back on land with a "strövkår" (like hun
2 CONC ting units or guerrilla) burn the then Danish cities Laholm, Engelholm and Bastad and the surrounding countryside. As early as May 15 he sailed from Dalarö as admiral and destroyed a hostile flotilla at the Pomeranian coast and in
2 CONC jagade consternation in Copenhagen by diving into the Sound . On June 4, he hit together with the Unified Danish- Lübeck fleet outside Buckow. Without definitively ruling returned the enemy of the Sound, then the horn for a time d
2 CONC ominated the Baltic Sea, procured a variety of ships and ravaged Mon. When the enemy returned the ports was July 7 a bloody battle between Rügen and Bornholm. The losses were great on both sides, but the Danes were larger and they
2 CONC  lost including its two flagship. A watch sailing fleet in the fall met no enemy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On May 23, 1566 the fleet sailed from Elfsnabben with a large number of ships, and, as before, he procured a variety of vessels, took the duty of others - this time without opposition in the Sound. After having brought home the ma
2 CONC ny hijacked merchant ships to Dalarö, he sailed again on 15 July and met July 26 with the main enemy again: the Danish and Lübeck fleet. Substituting kanonader but parted without judgment. Enemy ships went to Gotland , where they 
2 CONC were destroyed by a storm, and the Swedes returned to Elfsnabben. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The final journey 
2 CONT
2 CONT Now Horn was commissioned by King Erik XIV to surprise Halmstad, which Horn this time were hesitant to. On the way there, in Aby deanery in Östergötland , he died in the plague September 9, 1566. His death was a great loss to Swed
2 CONC en and King Erik. Several ships are named after him sjöhjälte. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He is buried in Uppsala Cathedral . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Trivia
2 CONT
2 CONT Several ships have been named after Klas Horn: 
2 CONT
2 CONT The ship Klas Horn who served in the Finnish Navy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The torpedo cruiser HMS Claes Horn as tjänstgjordei Swedish navy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Destroyer Class Horn that died at Horsfjärdskatastrofen . 
