2 _MARNM Hand
1 NAME Håkan Pedersson /Hand/ till Hagelsrum
2 GIVN Håkan Pedersson
2 SURN Hand
2 NSFX till Hagelsrum
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1485
2 ADDR
3 CITY Alingsås
3 STAE Västra Götalands län
3 CTRY Sweden
1 DEAT
2 DATE 14 FEB 1531
2 ADDR
3 CITY Attorp, Södra Säm
3 STAE Västergötland
3 CTRY Sverige
1 OCCU Ståthållare
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Håkan Pedersson, till Hagalsrum (Nr. 59)=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Also known as Haken Pedersson, till Hagelsrum and Dansjo samt Attorp and Tranetorp i Westergothland'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Peder Pedderson, till Hagalsrum and Christina Håkansdotter af Wangaslagten
2 CONT * Birth:	1485in Alingsås, Västra Götalands län, Sweden
2 CONT * Death:	February 14, 1531 (45-46) in Attorp, Södra Säm, Älvsborgs län, Västergötland, Sverige (Sweden)
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT *Married (1)  before 1514 with [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003897399378&photo_id=6000000118090728821&position=0 '''Kerstin Håkansson (Tun),'''] daughter Of gallowglass Håkan Karlsson Tun and 
2 CONC Ingrid Knutsdotter (Sparre over star).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Gertrud Håkansdotter,''' deceased in 1585. Married 1544-12-29 at the Royal Palace, with the Knight and Privy Council Herman Fleming.
2 CONT *''' Knut Håkansson,''' Field Colonel. Died 1565. (son of Håkan Pedersson Died 1565-10-20 (Killed in battle at Axtorna). Commander-in-Chief (Field Marshal) for all equestrian teams in Småland and Field Colonel for the Occupation A
2 CONC rmy in Blekinge. Became commander in 1554 over Östbo, Yästbo and Sunnerbo and in 1564-65 held several important commands in the war against Denmark. He led a ravaging train to Halland in January 1564, fought in July against Daniel
2 CONC  Kantzau in Småland and in September became field captain in Blekinge. In 1565 he first served as a "field marshal" (equestrian commander) in Småland and in the summer made a field commander in Halland, where (on August 16) he bur
2 CONC ned Falkenberg. After the other Swedish army came down, the conquest of Varberg (September 15) participated and led a division of footmen in the unfortunate battle of the Swedes at Axtorna, where he fell during the retreat. Marrie
2 CONC dabout 1550 with Märta Arvidsdotter (Drake) , daughter of the gunner Arvid Olofsson Drake and Brita Persdotter ( Hård af Segerstad ).
2 CONT * '''Brita Håkansdotterdotter Tun,''' Jöns Bosson Oxehufvud,  son of Bo Andersson &  Ingrid Jönsdotter and had Issue, daughter Märta Jönsdotter, died in childbirth 1569-04-25. Married 1568-06-27 in Älmestad to the Riksrådet and th
2 CONC e governor Peder Svensson Ribbing in his 1st marriage, born 1544, died 1604.
2 CONT * '''Barbro Håkansdotter,''' married 1: O With Häradshövdingen Olof Mattsson Kafle. Married 2: O With the merchant of the New Lödöse Harald Larsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Adelsvapen Hand nr #59 - http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Hand_nr_59#TAB_2
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=
2 CONT
2 CONT II.a) HÅKAN PEDERSSON, to Attorp in Säms sn, Årem in Daltorps sn, Trantorp in Örby sn, etc. (all in Älvsb.), Sealed together with his brother-in-law in the district governor of Kind Knut Håkansson (Tun) two of this issued parchmen
2 CONC t letters, dated Göråkra 26/2 1514 and so on. 26/3, received 20/3 1521 letter of attachment on the farm Bulem in Kinds herad, which he bought from the King's bailiff Staffan Bagge, regularly listed in the 1520s among the rust-serv
2 CONC ing Västgöta nobility, received 13/5 1525 in extension of King Gustaf Limmared in Tranemo sn (Älvsb.) and other farms, which the gunman Lasse Nilsson Skume had as county by the crown, proved the Riksdag in Västerås in 1527, was st
2 CONC ill alive in 1529, but was probably dead 14/2 1531, when another person received the above fief. - G 1: if before 1514 m CHRISTINA HÅKANSDOTTER (TUN), dtr t the gunman Håkan Karlsson (Tun), to Attorp and Erikstad who in the weapon
2 CONC  led an upright crescent against two stars, o Ingrid Knutsdotter (Drake af Intorp). (1) (3)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Håkan Pedersson to Hagelsrum, Dansjö, Attorp and Tranetorp, Västergötland and Åremma in Ölsremma parish, Älvsborg county. Also owned the Hulud farm.  Source: Supplement to The Introductory Swedish nobility's pedigrees in 2008 an
2 CONC d the Swedish biographical lexicon
2 CONT
2 CONT * About the genus Hand. Hand was a Swedish noble family descended from the savior Håkan Persson in Västergötland, died about 1530. His son was the High White Knut Håkansson, who distinguished himself in the Russian war in the 1550
2 CONC s and during the Nordic Seven Years' War and died in the battle of Axtorna on October 20, 1565. , the bailiff and county governor Håkan Knutsson (dead 1595 or 1596), was married to Erik XIV's extramarital daughter Virginia Eriksdo
2 CONC tter and was the father of Colonel Erik Hand (dead 1632) who was wounded and captured during the fighting outside Nuremberg in the summer of 1632 and died in captivity.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Håkan Knutsson's and Virginia Eriksdotter's daughter Elisabeth Hand (born 1588, died April 10, 1651) was first married to Duke Johan of Östergötland and later married the Lieutenant Colonel Per Jönsson (died March 19, 1664), who
2 CONC  in 1632 was named Gyllenswaard and became the ancestor of the family. with that name. Their daughter, Virginia Gyllenswaard, was married to Johan Gustafsson Örnevinge.
2 CONT
2 CONT * A son of Knut Håkansson, Arvid Knutsson, called himself Drake and that family was introduced to the Knights House under the name Drake af Hagelsrum.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.rotter.se/faktabanken/rotterarkivet/efterlysningar/1217-efterlysningar-1000-1099 Online Magazine RÖTTER]
2 CONT
2 CONT
